This fork of xv6 implements:
* sys_ps syscall: Retrieves list of process PIDs
* sys_pinfo syscall: Retrieves info about a certain process
* kernel processes (via minimal patching of scheduler and traps)
    - Also added a kernel-level reaper (although it can be repurposed) that can be used for testing purposes (testing kernel-level scheduling, testing kernel oops's triggered by processes without having to patch system calls)
* better panic behaviour (other cores will also spin on first printf or syscall)
* implemented kernel oops
    - The current process is terminated. If none, panic()
    - When any core attempts to acquire spinlocks previously held by this process, panic()
    - When any core attempts to acqurie sleeplocks previously held by this process, they can steal the sleeplocks
* implemented assertions to verify valid environment
